(7017762, 1062989, 83313, '<td valign="top">Deducting pointage for Japanese parts on an Italian frame. Unless it''s actually a Japanese made Bianchi frame. Then you get extra points for being ironic and all matchy-matchy. Campy parts on a Japanese frame would get a 10 for the improvement. But last I knew, Suntour isn''t an Italian make. Or rather, WASN''T, since they went out of business quite a few years back.<br/> <br/>I''m so confused.</td>', 'Deducting pointage for Japanese parts on an Italian frame. Unless it''s actually a Japanese made Bianchi frame. Then you get extra points for being ironic and all matchy-matchy. Campy parts on a Japanese frame would get a 10 for the improvement. But last I knew, Suntour isn''t an Italian make. Or rather, WASN''T, since they went out of business quite a few years back. I''m so confused.', '2013-04-10 15:20:39.000000', NULL, 1),
