(7021921, 1063286, 20799, '<td valign="top">I''ve missed your photographic dreams :-). Beautiful, congrats on the red and happy anniversary!</td>', 'I''ve missed your photographic dreams :-). Beautiful, congrats on the red and happy anniversary!', '2013-04-17 04:31:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7021923, 1062705, 20799, '<td valign="top">Well done! Is this on a runway? Great action, congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'Well done! Is this on a runway? Great action, congrats on the ribbon!', '2013-04-17 04:32:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7021924, 1063465, 20799, '<td valign="top">Fantastic light. Good to see you back on the front page, John.</td>', 'Fantastic light. Good to see you back on the front page, John.', '2013-04-17 04:34:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7021926, 1063581, 20799, '<td valign="top">Well done, I think you didn''t go wrong with the lighting.</td>', 'Well done, I think you didn''t go wrong with the lighting.', '2013-04-17 04:37:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7021930, 1062705, 100495, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tome:</b></div><hr/><i> Well done! Is this on a runway? Great action, congrats on the ribbon! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Tome<br/> <br/>Yes, I was lucky enough to get the use of a section of airfield for a couple of hours. When I arrived I immediately got a puncture so I had to walk half a mile home to change wheels as I''d removed my spare tube when I packed all my camera gear. I then took about 150 shots in various positions using a 18" long boom attached to the seat post and my 10-22mm lens at 10mm. When I got home I was quite disappointed with almost all of them and I didn''t have a shot good enough to submit, so I went back to take some more. The trouble was that, even on a flat surface, there was enough ''wobble'' in the boom to produce unwanted blur and soften the sharpness of the bike, but I narrowed down what set up looked best and I preferred the landscape format as it provided space for the bike to ride into.<br/> <br/>On the second batch I took another 150+ images, trying to get the sun in the right position and taking enough that I''d eventually get one I was really happy with. I think that as a keen cyclist I had an exact image in my head and I wasn''t getting it, but when I got home and had a look at the second batch there were 2 or 3 that were contenders. <br/> <br/>I was lucky being able to get use of the airfield and with the position of the sun, and the fct that the sun came out at all. <br/> <br/>Thanks for all the comments. I don''t think I will top this score.</td>', 'Originally posted by tome: Well done! Is this on a runway? Great action, congrats on the ribbon!   Hi Tome Yes, I was lucky enough to get the use of a section of airfield for a couple of hours. When I arrived I immediately got a puncture so I had to walk half a mile home to change wheels as I''d removed my spare tube when I packed all my camera gear. I then took about 150 shots in various positions using a 18" long boom attached to the seat post and my 10-22mm lens at 10mm. When I got home I was quite disappointed with almost all of them and I didn''t have a shot good enough to submit, so I went back to take some more. The trouble was that, even on a flat surface, there was enough ''wobble'' in the boom to produce unwanted blur and soften the sharpness of the bike, but I narrowed down what set up looked best and I preferred the landscape format as it provided space for the bike to ride into. On the second batch I took another 150+ images, trying to get the sun in the right position and taking enough that I''d eventually get one I was really happy with. I think that as a keen cyclist I had an exact image in my head and I wasn''t getting it, but when I got home and had a look at the second batch there were 2 or 3 that were contenders.  I was lucky being able to get use of the airfield and with the position of the sun, and the fct that the sun came out at all.  Thanks for all the comments. I don''t think I will top this score.', '2013-04-17 04:44:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7021934, 1062705, 108580, '<td valign="top">Super a-typical bicycle shot. Effort well rewarded.</td>', 'Super a-typical bicycle shot. Effort well rewarded.', '2013-04-17 04:58:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7021935, 1063467, 108580, '<td valign="top">When I read "bike" challenge I immediately thought motorbike. I was disappointed to see so few motorbikes. This however stood out. The freedom of the open road. WD.</td>', 'When I read "bike" challenge I immediately thought motorbike. I was disappointed to see so few motorbikes. This however stood out. The freedom of the open road. WD.', '2013-04-17 05:00:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7021936, 1062672, 50641, '<td valign="top">Very very cool...!</td>', 'Very very cool...!', '2013-04-17 05:02:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7021938, 1063319, 108580, '<td valign="top">Just for the record: When I read "bike" challenge I immediately thought motorbike. I was disappointed to see so few motorbikes. This however stands out in the quality stakes WD on superb light and processing. (yes Oliver is right but it''s forgiveable)<br/> <br/>I often have those thoughts especially when I see my true in the wild wildlife work (hours and days of patience) being deep 6''d by DNMC police and thus I connected with this :)<br/> <br/>"Second, there will be DNMC storm troopers who will say, this isnt a bike, its a motorcycle for Schwinns sake. To them I say, balderdash! Not the first expletive that occurred to me, but I digress. This was a Bikes challenge. Weve had Bicycles and Bicycles II. This was Bikes, not Bicycles III. And this is clearly a hot sports bike  my sport bike to be specific. So get over it. Of course by the time you read this, it will be too late to get over it  so this paragraph is here solely to make DNMC police feel guilty and to entertain the rest of you." <br/> <br/>Well said! I was entertained :)<br/></td>', 'Just for the record: When I read "bike" challenge I immediately thought motorbike. I was disappointed to see so few motorbikes. This however stands out in the quality stakes WD on superb light and processing. (yes Oliver is right but it''s forgiveable) I often have those thoughts especially when I see my true in the wild wildlife work (hours and days of patience) being deep 6''d by DNMC police and thus I connected with this :) "Second, there will be DNMC storm troopers who will say, this isnt a bike, its a motorcycle for Schwinns sake. To them I say, balderdash! Not the first expletive that occurred to me, but I digress. This was a Bikes challenge. Weve had Bicycles and Bicycles II. This was Bikes, not Bicycles III. And this is clearly a hot sports bike  my sport bike to be specific. So get over it. Of course by the time you read this, it will be too late to get over it  so this paragraph is here solely to make DNMC police feel guilty and to entertain the rest of you."  Well said! I was entertained :)', '2013-04-17 05:10:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7021945, 1063465, 96751, '<td valign="top">Folks, this is not a real town. Don''t get duped by this French guy, who actually uses a Hollywood set for these images :-)<br/> <br/>Congrats, John. Nice of the crew to leave that one spotlight on for you.</td>', 'Folks, this is not a real town. Don''t get duped by this French guy, who actually uses a Hollywood set for these images :-) Congrats, John. Nice of the crew to leave that one spotlight on for you.', '2013-04-17 05:22:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7021946, 1063565, 20799, '<td valign="top">Well done Alex, love the processing - in fact I think I recognized it :).</td>', 'Well done Alex, love the processing - in fact I think I recognized it :).', '2013-04-17 05:24:02.000000', NULL, 0),
